 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Local network resources
+
+Open **Local network** in the footer (`/devtools-times/local-network`) to read an HTTP(S) resource from a LAN device or a loopback service. Select the address space, enter the URL, and click **Connect and read resource**. Requests run in the user's browser, so localhost refers to their computer, not the application server.
+
+Deploy the application over HTTPS. Supporting browsers request local network or loopback permission; denied access can be restored in browser site settings. Browsers without the permission API still attempt the connection on click, subject to their network and mixed-content rules. The target service must return a standard CORS `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header allowing the application's origin. No deprecated Private Network Access preflight headers are required.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
